BUILT ON TUIPET
---------------

digibuddy is a companion for tuipet (https://github.com/joeltco/tuipet),
Copyright (c) 2026 Joel Taylor, released under the MIT License.

The export scripts in tools/ import tuipet's package directly
(tools/export_sprites.py uses `from tuipet import data, egg`;
tools/export_digidex.py uses `from tuipet import data, lines`), so tuipet's
MIT copyright notice must travel with any redistribution of this repository.
digibuddy resolves and reads tuipet's save.json read-only; it never writes to
it, and no save file is distributed with this repository.

WHAT THE MIT LICENSE DOES NOT COVER
-----------------------------------

digibuddy ships no game assets of its own. The audio and sprite files it
loads at runtime are derived from DVPet (https://theundersigned.itch.io/dvpet),
a Digimon fan game, and from the Digimon franchise (© Bandai). Those assets
are the property of their respective owners and are NOT licensed here:

- public/sounds/*.wav — 35 files, byte-identical copies of tuipet's data/sounds.
- public/sprites.json — sprite atlas extracted from tuipet's game data.
- public/digidex.json — knowledge exported from tuipet's data (creature names,
  evolution lines, care rules). Creature names are © Bandai.

Regenerate sprites and digidex from your own copy of tuipet with:

    python tools/export_sprites.py
    python tools/export_digidex.py

